course: dictionary
lesson: 14363
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant. The word operative can mean working, a worker, a secret agent, or something to do with a medical operation. «The new alarm system is now operative.» Here operative means working and in action.
explain: «The factory operative checked every machine before lunch.» Now operative is a noun, and it means a worker who works the machines. Same spelling, different meaning. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the sentence? Then try it in the sentence to check.
explain: «The operative slipped past the guards at midnight.» In a spy story, an operative is a secret agent on a mission. The words guards, midnight and slipped past are the clues. A word can change its meaning, but the words around it show you which meaning to use.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: Operative can be an adjective (working, in action) or a noun (a worker, or a secret agent).
fact: An operative is a worker who works machines, especially in a factory.
fact: Post-operative means after a medical operation, as in «post-operative care». Pre-operative means before one.
fact: «The operative word» means the most important word in a sentence.
exercise: «The new alarm system is now operative.» What does operative mean here? | *Working and in action | Broken and useless | Hidden under the ground | Very, very old
exercise: «The factory operative checked every machine before lunch.» What is an operative in this sentence? | A famous singer | A teacher | A type of cloud | *A worker who runs machines
exercise: In «Never touch the hot wire», which is the operative word? | Wire | *Never | The | Touch
test: «She needed post-operative care after her surgery.» What does post-operative mean? | *After the operation | During a birthday party | Before the operation | Without any doctors
test: In «The operative slipped past the guards at midnight», what is an operative? | A tired gardener | A kind teacher | A stone wall | *A secret agent on a mission
exam: «The spy was a skilled operative on a secret mission.» What does operative mean here? | A doctor who does operations | A kind of bird | *A secret agent | A worker in a sunny garden
